Have your clothes tailored to fit you, you don't have to waste a lot of money on expensive labels as a $200 well tailored suit will look way better than a $1000 poorly fitted suit.  Start with foundation pieces, pieces you can wear often and multiple ways and then expand out into things that you like that are your style but the number one thing is make sure they fit.

&nbsp;

Edit: people with money don't wear labels or at least not loud obvious labels, if you have money nobody cares that you have a luxury brand bag, they could have a luxury brand bag too if they wanted one.

I think he is a decent man and a good politician, which we'll need if we want to get anything done.  I also think he has strong foreign policy cred and the next president will have to repair all the bridges the previous administration has set on fire and then shit on.  He's behind the times a bit but not in a malicious way and I think that is comforting to the older crowd.  That being said he is reasonable and has shown that he can and does change his mind and does good things, he was very involved in the LGBT issues in the military as well as women's rights.  I also like Jill and I say this because Good presidents tend to have really good wives (see the former presidents).  We shall see what the voters have to say, there are a few really good candidates and a bunch of people who are just running to get their names out there, which is also good -it builds a deeper bench. 

&amp;#x200B;

Last thing is while removing the previous leader from office is job one a very close second is taking the Senate and not enough people are concerned about this.  I'm not so worried that the next Democratic president won't immediately implement M4A because that isn't his job, it's the job of congress.  We'll need a strong liberal congress and if that congress can deliver bills to the presidents desk, that Democratic president is going to sign those bills.  If the Dems don't take both houses just expect 4 years of grid lock and screaming from a major conservative news network.

This should be higher. I totally get the aversion to pumping iron but for a lot of people especially young guys it's as much a social thing as it is a working out thing. In my opinion the OPs cousin isn't saying let's go lift weights as much as he's saying let's hang out.  

&nbsp;

If the OP doesn't want to hang out with his cousin he doesn't have to but he is family and you will be seeing the dude for the next 50-ish years so having some sort of connection isn't a bad thing.

The selling of cannabis anywhere in the US is illegal federally. At anytime the US Marshalls can show up at any state licensed dispensary or grow house, shut it down and take everything to a field and burn it. Under Obama he told the DOJ to stand down and let the states handle it. Under Trump it's a bit more in limbo as the first AG was very anti-cannabis and Barr is no fan, we shall see.  

&nbsp;

Biden changing cannabis from a schedule 1 to a schedule 2 drug because very simply a schedule 1 drug is illegal period where a schedule 2 drug is not. This is a good thing because then the US Marshalls can't show up on your door step and burn all your plants, it give the states a lot more power.

